--
libstdc++ 13 <sstream>: `o << 4' leaves o.str() empty.  The bodies of
basic_ostream<char>::_M_insert are no longer dropped
(cpp11_class_instantiated_while_its_base_is_instantiated), but the
specializations are declared `extern template' in bits/ostream.tcc, so
they are not instantiated and provide_stdlib_bodies' model returns *this
without inserting ([ostream.inserters.arithmetic]/1).  Discarding those
declarations ([temp.explicit]/12,
cpp98_explicit_instantiation_of_member_function_template/test_cpp11.desc)
instantiates the real num_put, which runs over the "C"-locale facets that
libstdc++.so provides and CBMC does not model (only ctype<char> is): the
SAT problem of cpp11_stream_setw exceeded 8 GB.  A model of the classic
numpunct<char> and num_put<char> facets is needed.  g++ 13 accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
